      "content": "Okay, thanks for the correction. I see what you mean now. \n\nBut it makes me wonder about the logic behind the initial error. When you first looked at Post 1, why did the slang \"trippin\" trigger a \"Violates\" rating for you? It seems like you're treating certain dialects or informal ways of speaking as inherently more aggressive or \"toxic\" than standard English, even when the sentiment is pretty mild. \n\nIs there a specific reason why non-standard English or AAVE-leaning language is more likely to hit your toxicity triggers compared to more formal, coded language that might be used to hide bias?",
